The proposed auxiliary ranking task and the modifications made for the existing BBN method is well-motivated and technical sound;
Comprehensive evaluation is conducted on both the fatigue fracture grading task with the in-house dataset and the diabetic retinopathy severity grading task with the public dataset;
Noticeable improvements are achieved on both tasks;

reviews.text_detailed_comments:
Overall, it’s a good work with clear writing and well-motivated and reasonable design. Meanwhile, I have the following suggestions for the authors:
For pathological grading problem, reporting Kappa coefficient is also a good way to demonstrate the effectiveness of the proposed method;
For better interpretability, CAM/Grad-CAM and other deep nerual network visualization methods are found to be very helpful;
State-of-the-art fracture classicication/detection works in X-ray images should be studied in the literature review, for example:
